  <notepads>
    <notepad>
      <note>build_knowledge_base - loads the Larkspur documents in ../docs into the pgvector table kb_chunks, one
row per chunk.
Needs Ollama with nomic-embed-text, the pcm-pgvector container (localhost:5433) and a GENAI-EE
license.

1. gfn-docs: Get File Names, folder ${Internal.Entry.Current.Directory}/../docs, regular expression
   .*\.(pdf|docx|txt)$.
2. doc-read: Read Unstructured Document, Source Stream, File field name filename, Result Field name
   doc_text.
3. seg-chunks: AI Segmentation, doc_text, Split by Recursion, Using Tokens (Ollama, ${MODEL_NAME}),
   Max Segment size 300, Max Overlap size 30, output chunk with its index.
4. frmla-chunk-id: Formula, chunk_id = [short_filename] &amp; "#" &amp; [index] (String), a stable ID per chunk.
5. emb-chunks: Text to Vector, Stream, Input Text Field chunk, Embedding ID field chunk_id, metadata
   short_filename as source and index as chunk_index, Ollama nomic-embed-text at ${OLLAMA_URL}, input
   text included in the metadata.
6. vw-kb: Vector Writer, PGVector ${PG_HOST}:${PG_PORT}/${PG_DATABASE}, table kb_chunks, vector
   embedding, ID embedding_id, text chunk, metadata embedding_metadata, Upsert, create if missing,
   dimension 768, stored ID in stored_id.
7. sv-load-log: Select values, chunk_id, index, stored_id, embedding_dimensions.
8. txt-load-log: Text file output, kb_load_log.csv beside this file, fields at minimal width.

Run it again at any time: the same chunk keeps the same ID, so the table is updated, not doubled.
Parameters default to the lab kit (PG_PORT 5433, user and password genai).</note>
      <xloc>160</xloc>
      <yloc>32</yloc>
      <width>624</width>
      <heigth>422</heigth>
      <fontname>Segoe UI</fontname>
      <fontsize>10</fontsize>
      <fontbold>N</fontbold>
      <fontitalic>N</fontitalic>
      <fontcolorred>0</fontcolorred>
      <fontcolorgreen>0</fontcolorgreen>
      <fontcolorblue>0</fontcolorblue>
      <backgroundcolorred>167</backgroundcolorred>
      <backgroundcolorgreen>224</backgroundcolorgreen>
      <backgroundcolorblue>245</backgroundcolorblue>
      <bordercolorred>100</bordercolorred>
      <bordercolorgreen>100</bordercolorgreen>
      <bordercolorblue>100</bordercolorblue>
      <drawshadow>Y</drawshadow>
    </notepad>
  </notepads>
  <order>
